{% macro greet_doc() -%}
Return a greeting for a non-empty display name.
{% if docstring_resolved == 'google' %}
Args:
    name: Display name to greet.

Returns:
    A greeting in the form ``Hello, <name>!``.

Raises:
    ValueError: If ``name`` is blank after surrounding whitespace is removed.
{% elif docstring_resolved == 'numpy' %}
Parameters
----------
name : str
    Display name to greet.

Returns
-------
str
    A greeting in the form ``Hello, <name>!``.

Raises
------
ValueError
    If ``name`` is blank after surrounding whitespace is removed.
{% elif docstring_resolved == 'sphinx' %}
:param name: Display name to greet.
:returns: A greeting in the form ``Hello, <name>!``.
:raises ValueError: If ``name`` is blank after surrounding whitespace is removed.
{% else %}
The name is stripped of surrounding whitespace. A blank name is rejected with
``ValueError``; otherwise the result has the form ``Hello, <name>!``.
{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}

